# Symbulator circuit book

title: Circuits for Lesson 8 of the Tutorial

[AS7's Example 11.5 (maximum average power)]

e,1,0,10
r1,1,2,4
r2,2,0,8-6j
r3,2,3,5j

analysis: ac
omega: omega
tool: th
n1: 3
n2: 0
note: The load that draws the most power is the conjugate of zeq. Version 9 has no separate apmax: in AC, pmax is already the average maximum power.
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
rms: no
polar: no


[AS7's Example 11.10 (power factor)]

e,1,0,30
r1,1,2,6
r2,2,0,-2j
r3,2,0,4

analysis: ac
omega: omega
note: The power factor comes from the pf mini-tool, given ve and -ie: 0.97342 leading. The minus sign matters -- ie is the current into the source, and without it the tool says lagging.
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
rms: yes
polar: no
evaluate: -pe


[AS7's Example 11.13 (complex power)]

e,1,0,220
r1,1,2,4+2j
r2,2,0,15-10j

analysis: ac
omega: omega
rounding: 5
si: no
units: yes
rms: yes
polar: no
evaluate: -se


